      "text": "To give you the best recommendation, I need to know what you are trying to block from syncing. The term \"sync blocker\" can refer to several different things.\n\nHere are the four most common solutions based on what you might be looking for:\n\n### 1. Cloud Storage Sync (OneDrive, Dropbox, Google Drive)\nIf you want to stop files from automatically uploading to the cloud:\n*   **The \"Pause\" Method:** Most apps (OneDrive, Dropbox, Google Drive) have a \"Pause syncing\" option if you right-click their icon in the Taskbar (Windows) or Menu Bar (Mac).\n*   **Selective Sync:** Go into the app settings and uncheck specific folders you don\u0027t want synced to your computer.\n*   **Insync:** A powerful third-party tool that gives you much more granular control over what gets synced and when.\n\n### 2. Browser Sync (Chrome, Edge, Safari)\nIf you want to prevent your history, passwords, and tabs from following you to other devices:\n*   **Chrome:** Go to `Settings` \u003e `You and Google` \u003e `Sync and Google Services` \u003e `Manage what you sync` and turn off \"Sync everything.\"\n*   **Edge:** Go to `Settings` \u003e `Profiles` \u003e `Sync` and turn it off.\n*   **Privacy Extension:** Use **uBlock Origin**. While primarily an ad blocker, it prevents \"third-party sync\" trackers that follow you across different websites.\n\n### 3. Programming \u0026 Software Development\nIf you are a developer looking for a way to manage \"Synchronous\" vs \"Asynchronous\" code (preventing race conditions):\n*   **Mutex/Locks:** Use a **Mutex** (Mutual Exclusion) or **Semaphore** to \"block\" a thread from accessing a resource while another thread is using it.\n*   **JavaScript:** Use `await` to block the execution of an `async` function until a promise resolves.\n*   **Python:** Use `threading.Lock()` to prevent multiple threads from syncing data simultaneously.\n\n### 4. Productivity \u0026 App Blocking\nIf you want to \"block\" your phone or computer from syncing new emails/notifications so you can focus:\n*   **Cold Turkey (Windows/Mac):** The most powerful blocker for stopping apps and websites from communicating with servers.\n*   **Freedom (All platforms):** Allows you to block \"Sync\" processes and internet access across all devices simultaneously.\n*   **Focus Mode (iOS/Android):** Built-in settings that stop background data sync and notifications for specific apps during set hours.\n\n---\n\n**Which one of these fits your situation?** (e.g., \"I want to stop my phone from syncing photos,\" or \"I need a code snippet to block a process.\")",
